.TH EUCLID-CLI-EDS-DELETE-ZONE 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.3.2" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eds-delete-zone \- delete a zone and every record in it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eds delete-zone
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I ZONE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a zone and every record set in it. There is no undo: what the
zone held is gone when this returns.
.PP
The server stops answering for the zone at once. What a question about
one of its names gets afterwards depends on what is left: an enclosing
zone answers it from its own records, and with none it is forwarded or
refused like any name EDS does not hold.
.PP
Resolvers that cached an answer from the zone keep it for up to that
record's TTL, and a negative answer for up to the zone's TTL. Lowering
the zone's TTLs a while before deleting it is how to make the change
land quickly everywhere.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fIZONE\fR
The zone's apex. Required.
.SH OUTPUT
A JSON object with
.IR deletedRecords ,
the number of record sets that went with the zone.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The zone was deleted.
.TP
.B 1
No such zone in your account (HTTP 404), or a grant does not allow
deleting it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eds delete-zone --name lab.corp.example
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eds (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-create-zone (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-delete-record (1)
